      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Navigating a roof insurance claim in Utah requires acting quickly within your policy's timeframe (typically 1 year from the storm date) and working with local professionals to document damage.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "requires acting quickly within your policy's timeframe (typically 1 year from the storm date) and working with local professionals to document damage"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "\ud83d\udcc5 Step-by-Step Action Plan"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Immediate Inspection : Hire a trusted local roofer (like Bob Harvey Roofing, Legacy Roofing, or Eagle Rock Roofing) to document storm impacts with photos before cleanup .",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              2,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Policy Review: Check whether your policy uses Actual Cash Value (ACV) , which factors in depreciation, or Replacement Cost Value (RCV).",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Filing the Claim: Contact your insurance carrier with the exact storm date, local weather reports, and your contractor's evidence.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Adjuster Meeting: Be present on-site when the insurance adjuster arrives, walking the roof alongside your roofing contractor to ensure no collateral damage (gutters, vents, flashing) is missed ."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          3,
          5
        ]
      },
